  "articleBody": "Thinking about a new bathroom vanity? While some simple swap-outs can be a DIY dream, there are definitely times when bringing in a professional just makes sense. You should absolutely consider calling in the pros if your vanity is wall-mounted. These can be trickier to install securely and get perfectly level than a floor-standing unit. Another big signal is if your plumbing needs to be moved. Relocating water lines or drains isn't a job for the faint of heart or the inexperienced; it often involves permits and specific tools. If you're looking at custom countertops that require precise templating, like granite or quartz, that’s another strong indicator. Getting those measurements and cuts just right is critical for a flawless fit. And, of course, if your project involves any electrical work, like adding new lighting or outlets near the vanity, it's always best to have a licensed electrician handle it. Essentially, if your vanity install is part of a broader bathroom remodel, involves complex changes, or if you just want peace of mind that it's done perfectly and leak-free, it's time to call a pro like HH Remodeling LLC. We handle the intricacies so you don't have to.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
